WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.365
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.060
 I felt like I was
just cast yesterday,

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.110
and now the show's out.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.420
And we're promoting it, and
I'm here with all my, you know,

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:14.260
people.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.850
And then I haven't
seen them in so long.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:17.170
 Such a huge celebration.

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:18.700
 It feels like
a family reunion.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:19.720
 It's like a dream.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.400
 I'm, like, still
taking this in.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.710
I feel like if I look around too
much, I'm going to freak out.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.670
 I'm really excited for the
world to meet Iman Vellani

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:33.620
and see her performance
as Kamala Khan

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.600
because it's absolutely the
heart and centaur of the show.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.160
And I think people
are going to love her.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.800
 Iman Vellani, she is
Kamala Khan, you know.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.870
She's the biggest Marvel
fan you can imagine.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.250
 It's being myself
on a larger scale.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.440
Like, I get to go to
work and play dress up.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.500
It's literally what I
did when I was a kid.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.590
And, so, yeah, it's quite easy.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:54.680
I just put a lot of my real
life into Kamala's character

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:56.923
and making her as
authentic as possible.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.290
 Are you sure that
you can keep that on?

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.090
 It's an homage.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:00.077
- It's a lawsuit.
- Great.

00:01:00.077 --> 00:01:01.610
Then I'll meet Captain
Marvel in court.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.750
Won't be the first case
in the American judiciary

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:04.550
to hug it out.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:06.010
 Our cast is-- it's so close.

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.010
And we're, like, best friends.

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.000
And everything you see on screen
is how it is in real life.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.450
And so just that
relationship and getting

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.910
to spend so much time with
these incredible people.

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:16.970
 When I have scenes
with Iman and Rish,

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:18.420
we just have so much fun.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:19.730
 I wish I had more
scenes with Saagar.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.030
Every time I'm with him, I just
break, and I start laughing.

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:24.800
 It's the camaraderie
of the cast.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.720
I mean, you know, we
all are best friends.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.310
 I'm very excited
for people finally--

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.780
because we've been working
on this for a very long time,

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.660
finally-- get to
me not just Kamala,

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:41.960
but the entire cast, and in
particular, her family, who

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.290
from the comics were such
a great ensemble and now

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.270
have been brought to
life in an amazing way.

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:50.720
 I wanted to layer as much
as I could a strong woman,

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:54.170
matriarch of her household
and is loving and kind,

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.610
but can throw down.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:59.000
 This is one family, Pakistani
immigrant family, in America.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.030
We just segue and
assimilate with everybody

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:02.930
else so beautifully.

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:04.280
So you'll see customs.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:05.840
You'll see religious festivals.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:07.440
 The Khan family is perfect.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.240
They really are.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.530
I want to be adopted by them.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:16.040
 Kamala Khan is a teenage girl.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:20.060
So she experiences all
of the same boy trauma.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.020
 Boys.

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:21.950
 Excuse me.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.120
 Yeah.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.170
 You're kind of on my shirt.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:25.070
 Sorry.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:25.910
 It's high school.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.520
You know, there's
always that drama bit.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.220
You know, Kamran comes in, and,
you know, Bruno sees him and is

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:32.610
like, who is this, you know?

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:33.410
And I don't know.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:36.030
It'll be cool for
the fans to see.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:39.320
And I think a lot of
teenagers will relate to it.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.200
 It starts out as a
story in Jersey City

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.810
and then expands to
the entire globe.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.750
 Having a show with this type
of representation in the MCU

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:51.380
is huge and people being
able to turn on Disney Plus

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.885
and see somebody that looks
just like them and, you know,

00:02:53.885 --> 00:02:55.730
find a different
character that they relate

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.160
to because I think we have
such a beautiful diverse group

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:58.967
of personalities.

00:02:58.967 --> 00:03:00.800
 You're not going to believe
what you're going to see.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.720
Marvel superheroes are bit.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:03.920
They're brawny.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.760
They're the corporate
giants, et cetera, et cetera.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.000
They're from other worlds.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.530
This is real world.

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:11.480
And real world has heroes.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:12.980
And you can be a hero too.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:16.600
Just believe because Marvel
will make you believe.

